    "prompt": "subject_definitions:\n<Location 1> is the empty place in the first frame: a sunlit stone courtyard: a pale plaster wall with black iron posts and a thin rail on a low stone ledge in front of it, olive trees and a terracotta pot, worn stone paving.\n\nsummary:\n[keyframe completion] 5 locked-off views of the same empty location, separated by hard cuts, for an environment reference sheet.\n\nretention_analysis:\n<Location 1> (appears in [Shot 1] through [Shot 5]): fully_preserved - The same walls, furniture, barrier, floor and light in every view. Only the camera position and direction change.\n\ndetailed_description:\nThe location is completely empty: no people and no animals, and nothing within it moves. Every shot is a locked-off static camera at eye level, the horizon level and centred, no camera movement of any kind, except the last, which looks straight down.\n[Shot 1] The first frame's view: from the open courtyard, looking at the pale plaster wall with the black iron posts and thin rail on a low stone ledge, the olive trees and a terracotta pot.\n[Shot 2] At 00:01.000, hard cut: from in front of the pale wall, behind the iron posts and rail, looking straight out across the open courtyard at its far side.\n[Shot 3] At 00:02.000, hard cut: from one end of the wall looking along it, the posts, the rail and the olive trees on one side, the open paving on the other.\n[Shot 4] At 00:03.000, hard cut: from the other end of the wall looking back along it.\n[Shot 5] At 00:04.000, hard cut to a straight-down view of the whole courtyard, like an architect's cutaway: the wall along the top edge, the posts and the rail in front of it, the paving below. Hold to the end. Each cut changes the camera instantly; the architecture stays fixed.\n\noverall_soundscape:\nA light breeze throughout.\n\nnon_diegetic_music:\nN/A",
